## Best Practices

### 1. Plugin Management

- **Always check availability** before using plugins
- **Handle initialization errors** gracefully
- **Clean up resources** when components unmount
- **Use TypeScript** for better type safety

### 2. Performance

- **Lazy load heavy components** on mobile
- **Optimize images** for mobile screens
- **Use native animations** when possible
- **Minimize bundle size** with tree shaking

### 3. User Experience

- **Respect platform conventions** (iOS vs Android)
- **Handle safe areas** properly
- **Provide loading states** for async operations
- **Implement proper error messages**

### 4. Security

- **Validate plugin inputs** before calling native methods
- **Handle sensitive data** securely
- **Use biometric authentication** when available
- **Implement proper key management**

### 5. Testing

- **Mock plugins** in unit tests
- **Test on real devices** for integration tests
- **Use platform-specific test suites**
- **Test error scenarios** thoroughly

## Common Patterns

### Plugin Wrapper Pattern

```typescript
// Create wrapper for complex plugins
class PluginWrapper {
  private plugin: any;
  private isAvailable: boolean = false;

  constructor(pluginName: string) {
    this.initializePlugin(pluginName);
  }

  private async initializePlugin(pluginName: string) {
    try {
      this.plugin = await import(`@capacitor/${pluginName}`);
      this.isAvailable = true;
    } catch (error) {
      console.warn(`Plugin ${pluginName} not available:`, error);
    }
  }

  async callMethod(method: string, ...args: any[]) {
    if (!this.isAvailable || !this.plugin[method]) {
      throw new Error(`Method ${method} not available`);
    }
    
    return this.plugin[method](...args);
  }
}
```

### Platform-Specific Components

```svelte
<!-- PlatformWrapper.svelte -->
<script>
  import { Capacitor } from '@capacitor/core';
  
  let { children, ios, android, web } = $props();
  
  const platform = Capacitor.getPlatform();
  
  $: platformContent = platform === 'ios' ? ios : 
                      platform === 'android' ? android : 
                      web;
</script>

{#if platformContent}
  {@render platformContent()}
{:else}
  {@render children()}
{/if}
